WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.302
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-, Grammy-,

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:06.272
Tony- and Academy Award-winning
actress, singer and producer,

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.840
and the host of
"The Jennifer Hudson Show,"

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.009
which airs every weekday.
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.045
our friend Jennifer Hudson,
everybody.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:29.028 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.497
Hello. Welcome back.
-Whoo!

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.099
[ Cheers and applause continue ]
-So happy you're here.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:36.269
-Thank you.
I'm happy to be here.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.604
-I think we're still
technically within the window

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.573
where I can talk
about Halloween costumes.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.675
Do you agree?
-Yeah, a little bit.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.245
-I mostly just want to talk
about you dressed up

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.714
like Missy Elliott
on your show

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.249
from the famous
"The Rain" video, right?

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:53.186
-Yes, I did.
-That's Missy. And you...

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.722
There was no -- I mean,
no shortcuts here.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.956
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.626
-No, we go all the way.
-You went all the way.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.127
This is not some last-minute

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.729
"I'm going to be Missy Elliott
going to a Halloween party."

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.264
Like, throwing a Hefty bag on
or something.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:06.866
-No.
-You just went the whole look.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.635
-The whole look. Yes, I did.
-And she saw it.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:10.670
-Yes, she did.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.071
-And she liked it.
-She loved it.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:16.475
-And she wrote, "You merked dat.
Whooty whoo.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.678
You won. I love you."
-That meant something good.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.179
-That's something good.
-It did.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:24.416
It came from Missy.
-I'll tell you this.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:26.185
I'm starting to come
to the conclusion that no one's

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:27.787
ever going to tell me
I merked anything.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.122
[ Laughter ]
-I don't know. If you dress --

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.124
-You're never too late to merk.

00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:34.594
We've talked
about artists that inspired you.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.295
Like Aretha last time
you were here.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.764
But Missy was someone
who inspired you

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.431
when you were younger.
-Oh, my God, yes.

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:41.401
I mean, Missy is a legend.
-She is a legend.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.035
-So I had to sneak it in there,
you know, like,

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:45.371
pay homage to her
with my Halloween costume.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.073
So I really thought I was her
in the moment.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.074
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.509
-I bet she's a very fun person

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.844
to think you are for a moment.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:54.247
-She is a fun person,
that's for sure.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.849
And somebody, you know,
to pay homage to.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.618
-It's really -- I mean,
it is a nice thing

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.386
that I think happens where
all of a sudden you realize,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.954
like someone, you know,

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.857
you listened to when you were
younger is now a legend.

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.659
You know, you were
like someone you were aware of

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:09.095
and your parents weren't.
-Right.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.163
-And then all of a sudden
you're like,

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.631
"Oh, and now they are just
a legend."

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.666
-Yes. And my kid wasn't aware

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.068
because he came with me
to work that day

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:18.771
when we -- I was in my Missyness
and he was like, "Who is that?"

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.907
He's like, "Oh, Mama, you ain't
going to be able to do that."

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.942
But I did it
and I pulled it off.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.378
-I can't believe you --
-You see my Missy skills, kid?

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.679
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:31.150
-I can't believe your son
doesn't think you can do it.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.718
-No. You know how kids are.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.286
They don't think you can do
anything.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:37.523
-Now, one thing you've done
since the last time you're here,

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:38.758
you were about to start
your talk show,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.526
and now you're
in your second season.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:44.263
Six Emmy nominations,
including best talk show.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.933
-How am I doing? Thank you.
-You're a natural.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:47.967
-Thank you.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.301
-You were saying
one of the interesting --

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.637
We were talking backstage that
now

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.404
that you actually have
your own talk show,

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:54.173
you realize when you're a guest
on a talk show

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.041
that everybody who in the past
just seemed

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:58.044
like they were running around,
they all serve a purpose.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.346
-Yes. You know,
now I get to understand.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.681
Yeah. Why all the people
running around,

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.849
what they doing,
who's talking to me,

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.751
what am I supposed to do
when I come out here,

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.353
you know, the whole field
because it's different now

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.522
being on the other side
as the host.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.156
And then it's weird again,
though,

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.759
but cool being the guest.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.926
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.395
I'm still trying
to make sense out of it.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.364
-Yeah. Did you -- Was there
a part of hosting a show

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.366
that you were most worried
about before you kicked it off?

00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:22.702
-You know what?

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.904
Speaking publicly, it's like
one of my biggest fears.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.774
-Oh.
-So to take it on and like,

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.242
"Oh, you want me to talk
to a whole audience?"

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.311
And the first, like --
when we first started the show,

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.680
we would go like in for prep,

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.815
and if I was singing,
then I would do a rehearsal

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:38.484
with the band
and then go and perform.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.353
If I was acting,
you work with an acting coach

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.654
and then you shoot a scene.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.323
With the talk show life,
I'm like, "So we're just going

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.059
to like, sit and keep talking?"

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.526
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.863
"Oh! That's what this is."
So that was surprising to me.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.331
-It's so funny. I would say,

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:55.435
of every fear,
a fear of public speaking,

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:58.303
I would have guessed would be
a deal breaker for this job.

00:03:58.303 --> 00:04:00.139
-You would think but, you know.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.542
-It's like, "Well, I freeze up
if I see camera or lights,

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:06.912
but other than that,
I'd love to take the job."

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:08.380
You seem very natural.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.115
And I mean, again,
one of the coolest things

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:11.150
about the job for me

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.018
is the people
you get to talk to

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:14.420
that you feel like maybe
you never would have

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.788
had a conversation
with otherwise.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.456
Is there anybody where
you've been talking to them

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.391
and thinking, "I can't believe
I'm here right now"?

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:22.594
-Oh, my God. Several people.
Like, I fan out on a lot.

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:25.732
Like, I got to sit
with Smokey Robinson.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.067
-That's a pretty good one.
-Talked to him.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.502
And sometimes
I want to scream like,

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.937
"Oh, my God, this is Smokey
sitting right here."

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:34.006
But then I'd be like,
"Ooh, let me be Mrs. Host."

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.308
Like, whatever that is
to keep my composure.

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:39.345
-It is a funny thing
when you talk to legends

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.382
because you do want to do that.
You do want to scream it,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.882
but you realize
they don't want to hear it

00:04:43.882 --> 00:04:45.952
because they also -- he knows
he's Smokey Robinson, you know?

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.287
He wasn't taking
advantage of the moment.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.256
So the weirdest thing
is how you actually

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.624
have to, like, pump the brakes
a little bit

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.193
on your own fandom for people.
-Right.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.796
To, you know,
be a host like yourself

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.599
and try to be polished
and, you know,

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.434
and not lose it and fan out.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.702
But that's who you want.
You know?

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.504
-Just try to always move
like a video game character.

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:08.241
-Welcome to "The
Jennifer Hudson Show," you know.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.443
-Yeah.
-How that's supposed to sound.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.977
-It's nice when they put
your name in the title.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.713
It makes it easier to remember.
Yeah, I love that.

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:16.282
I love that it's "Late Night
with Seth Meyers."

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.251
I'm like, "I'll forget a lot of
stuff, but that I can get."

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.553
Yeah. I have a lot more
to ask you.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.854
Will you stick around?
-Yes, I will.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.057
-We'll be right back
with more Jennifer after this.

